    "text": "<p>For a plane electromagnetic wave, the magnetic field at a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>&nbsp;and time&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math>&nbsp;is :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.2</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.5</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.5</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>.</p><p>The instantaneous electric field&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;corresponding to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;is :</p>"
